  "reply_text": "**One merge-blocking finding:**\n\n**[P1] View-only shares can edit unlocked documents — `src/guard.js:12`**\n\n`share.mask & WRITE === WRITE` is parsed as `share.mask & (WRITE === WRITE)`. Since that comparison is always `true`, it effectively checks bit `1` (`READ`), not bit `4` (`WRITE`).\n\nConfirmed:\n- A viewer (`READ`, mask `1`) **can edit**.\n- A read/comment share (mask `3`) **can edit**.\n- A write-only share (mask `4`) **cannot edit**.\n\nUse `hasRight(share.mask, WRITE) && !share.locked`, or parenthesize the bitwise expression.\n\nAll **6 existing tests pass**, but they miss this because the editor fixture has both READ and WRITE. Add cases for a viewer being denied editing and a WRITE-only share being allowed.\n\nNo other concrete defects found in the diff. **No files changed.**",
